# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context for the @cms/server image.
# Keep the build context small and deterministic; never ship .env,
# node_modules, or coverage state into the daemon.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build outputs
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.turbo
**/.vite

# Dependency trees — these are recreated inside the image by pnpm.
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.pnpm-debug.log*

# Local secrets and operator-only state.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12

# VCS, IDE noise, and macOS metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor / OS logs.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Test artefacts that should not affect the image.
**/test
**/tests
**/__tests__
**/vitest.config.ts
**/.vite

# Documentation, scratch and unrelated workspace glue that operators
# do not need in a production container. The image rebuilds from the
# lockfile so contributors can refresh locally as needed.
docs/
teach/
.gjc/
.scratch/
launchpad.log
*.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
artifacts/
handoff.md
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Compose and infrastructure artefacts are not part of the server image.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml
docker-compose*.yml
